course: dictionary
lesson: 1796
title: Clone: an exact copy
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A clone is an exact copy of another living thing, with the same genes. Context helps you see this: «In 2020 a Przewalski's horse foal called Kurt was cloned from cells frozen 40 years earlier.» Kurt was made from cells that came from another horse, so he is a copy of that horse.
explain: Look for clue words. «Exact copy» and «same genes» tell you that a clone is not just similar. Try the swap: put «copy» into the sentence in place of clone. «A grove of aspens can be one giant plant, all trunks joined by one root system with the same genes» still makes sense, so you know your meaning is right.
explain: Clone also works as a verb, meaning to make a copy, and as an informal word for something very like another. «A cheap clone of a famous game» is not a real copy of the game, just something that looks and plays very much like it. A computer can clone a disk in the same way.
fact: Clone (noun) means a living thing that is an exact copy of another, with the same genes.
fact: Clone (verb) means to make an exact copy of a living thing, or of a disk, phone or code project.
fact: Dolly the sheep was the first mammal cloned from an adult cell.
fact: Identical twins are natural clones, because they have the same genes.
fact: Informal: «a cheap clone» means something very like another thing, but not the real original.
exercise: What does clone mean as a noun? | A kind of food made from milk | A small wild animal that lives in trees | *A living thing that is an exact copy of another | A type of rock
exercise: «A cheap clone of a famous game» is an informal use. What does clone mean here? | A shop that sells cheap things | A fast car | *Something very like another | A game with no rules
exercise: «In 2020 a Przewalski's horse foal called Kurt was cloned from cells frozen 40 years earlier.» Find and copy the word that means a baby horse. | *foal | frozen | years | cells
test: What does it mean to clone something? | To sell it cheaply | To throw it away | To paint it a new colour | *To make an exact copy of it
test: «A grove of aspens can be one giant plant, all trunks joined by one root system with the same genes.» Why is the grove called a clone? | Its trunks were planted one at a time by people | Its trunks are all different colours | It grows in many different countries | *Its trunks have the same genes
exam: Dolly was a clone of an adult sheep, so what would be true of her? | She would be a completely new kind of animal | She would have no genes at all | *Her genes would match the sheep she was copied from | Her genes would be random and unlike the sheep's
